# Allowlist: the build context is only what the image needs. Everything else,
# including generated secrets (deploy/local/integration/secrets, tokens.env,
# deploy/local/kind/.state), .env, .venv, .git and Terraform state, never
# reaches the Docker daemon, so it can't be copied into an image by mistake.
# tests/test_repo_consistency.py pins this shape.
*
!pyproject.toml
!README.md
!requirements.lock
!src/
!deploy/routing.yaml
!deploy/pricing.yaml
!deploy/policy/
**/__pycache__
